<title>UK: DML to take over UK Devonport dockyard -local MP.</title>
<headline>DML to take over UK Devonport dockyard -local MP.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The UK government is set to announce imminently a deal to sell Devonport naval dockyard in Plymouth to Devonport Management Limited (DML), which has been running it since 1987, the local member of parliament said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Labour MP David Jamieson said he had a question on the matter on the parliamentary order to the Ministry of Defence which he expected to be answered later today.</p>
<p>A Ministry spokesman declined to confirm the deal, but said a government announcement on the future of the dockyard was likely either on Tuesday or Wednesday.</p>
</text>
